```java
public static boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
    // If base case fails, the number isn't a power of 3
    if (n <= 0) return false;

    int bitIndex = 0;
    while (n > 1) {
        // Shift 'n' right by 1 bit
        n >>= 1;

        // Increment the exponent as 1-bit position found
        bitIndex++;
    }

    // Check for exact power of 3, if bitIndex equals logbase 3 (approximately 1)
    double logBaseThree = Math.log1p(1.0) * bitIndex;
    return (Math.pow(3, logBaseThree) == (double) n);
}
```

This algorithm calculates the approximate logbase 3 for a power of 3 using the log1p(1+x) property and then checks if it matches the given integer.

However, note that this method has limited precision due to floating-point arithmetic imprecisions. For larger powers, consider using a loop-based approach instead, or using a recursive method with some care taken to avoid stack overflow.

